IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgm-part5-div4`

-- Tests of sgm-part5-div4.l4 (ss 189A to 196). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.
-- Dates are Date day month year. The trace clock counts days after the day of the event (AT 0).

§ `Fixtures`

`a full register of a company with a share capital` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a full register of a company with no share capital` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS FALSE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS FALSE

`a register with no names and addresses` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS FALSE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a register with no statement of shares` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a register with no amount paid` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a register with no date of entry as a member` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a register with no date of ceasing to be a member` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS FALSE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS TRUE

`a register with no allotment dates` MEANS `s 190(1) register entries` WITH
    `the register enters the names and addresses of the members` IS TRUE
    `the company has a share capital` IS TRUE
    `the register enters a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the member's holding` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date at which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member` IS TRUE
    `the register enters the date of every allotment of shares to members and the number of shares comprised in each allotment` IS FALSE

`the penalty of a fine of $1,000 and a default penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE
`the penalty of a fine of $400 and a default penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 400, 0, FALSE, TRUE

§ `s 189A`

-- 189A(1): "This Division applies only in relation to a public company." Expected: yes for a public company; the text's no ("only") for any other.
#ASSERT `s 189A(1) this Division applies to the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 189A(1) this Division applies to the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 189A(2): "means the register of members required to be kept by a public company under section 190(1)".
#ASSERT `s 189A(2) the register is the register of this Division` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 189A(2) the register is the register of this Division` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 190(1): the register and its entries`

#ASSERT `s 190(1) the company must keep a register of its members` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a company that is not public: s 189A(1) says the Division applies only to a public company, so the text says no
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the company must keep a register of its members` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a): names and addresses, and for a company having a share capital the statement of shares and amount paid
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` `a full register of a company with a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` `a full register of a company with no share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` `a register with no names and addresses` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` `a register with no statement of shares` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(a) the register enters the names and addresses and, for a company having a share capital, the statement of shares` `a register with no amount paid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b)
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(b) the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered as a member` `a full register of a company with a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(b) the register enters the date at which the name of each person was entered as a member` `a register with no date of entry as a member` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c)
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(c) the register enters the date at which a person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years ceased` `a full register of a company with a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(c) the register enters the date at which a person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years ceased` `a register with no date of ceasing to be a member` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): only "in the case of a public company having a share capital"
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(d) the register enters the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` `a full register of a company with a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(d) the register enters the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` `a register with no allotment dates` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(1)(d) the register enters the date and size of every allotment, for a company having a share capital` `a full register of a company with no share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1) as a whole
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` `a full register of a company with a share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` `a full register of a company with no share capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` `a register with no date of ceasing to be a member` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` `a register with no allotment dates` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register has every entry the subsection requires` `a register with no names and addresses` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the keel's seam: a public company's register of members is the register kept pursuant to section 190
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(1) the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 190(2): shares converted into stock`

-- converted and notice given: the company must alter the register
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- converted but no notice to the Registrar: the "where" gate is unmet, so the text's no
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the company must alter the register to show stock instead of shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the register has been altered as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(2) the register has been altered as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 190(2A): own shares bought under section 76H`

-- bought and not all cancelled at once: (1)(a), (b), (c) and (2) must be complied with
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(a) the requirements of subsections (1)(a), (b) and (c) and (2) must be complied with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- bought and all cancelled immediately under section 76K(1): "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(a) the requirements of subsections (1)(a), (b) and (c) and (2) must be complied with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no purchase: the "Where" gate is unmet
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(a) the requirements of subsections (1)(a), (b) and (c) and (2) must be complied with` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): a cancelled share is disregarded; the text says nothing of one not cancelled
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(b) the share or stock is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(b) the share or stock is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(2A)(b) the share or stock is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 190(3) and (4): former members and evidence`

#ASSERT `s 190(3) the public company may keep the names and particulars of former members separately` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(3) the public company may keep the names and particulars of former members separately` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- need not supply former members' names to an applicant for a copy, unless the applicant specifically asks for them
#ASSERT `s 190(3) the company need not supply the names and particulars of former members` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(3) the company need not supply the names and particulars of former members` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(3) the company need not supply the names and particulars of former members` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(4) the register is prima facie evidence of the matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(4) the register is prima facie evidence of the matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(4) the register is prima facie evidence of the matter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 190(5) and (6): the index`

-- "having more than 50 members": 50 is not more than 50; 51 is
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` 50 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` 51 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` 200 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index"
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` 51 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the public company must keep an index of the names of its members` 10 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made": register altered on 1 March 2026, last day 15 March 2026
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the last day for making the necessary alteration in the index` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
-- across the leap day of 2024: altered on 20 February 2024, last day 5 March 2024; in 2026, 6 March
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the last day for making the necessary alteration in the index` (Date 20 2 2024) EQUALS Date 5 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the last day for making the necessary alteration in the index` (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS Date 6 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the index was altered within 14 days after the alteration of the register` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 190(5) the index was altered within 14 days after the alteration of the register` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026))
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the index was altered within 14 days after the alteration of the register` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 190(5) the index was altered within 14 days after the alteration of the register` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 190(6) the index has the indication the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(6) the index has the indication the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 190(7): the offence`

#ASSERT `s 190(7) the public company is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the public company is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- default made, but this officer is not in default
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty": no imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the most the public company may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the penalty of a fine of $1,000 and a default penalty`
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the most the public company may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the most the officer of the company may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the penalty of a fine of $1,000 and a default penalty`
#ASSERT `s 190(7) the most the officer of the company may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules of section 190`

-- (1): no time limit, so it cannot be breached by lateness. EXPECT RESIDUAL for no events; FULFILLED when the company keeps the register.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 190(1) a public company must keep a register of its members` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 190(1) a public company must keep a register of its members` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 190(1) keep a register of its members and enter in it what the subsection requires` AT 3
-- (5), keep the index: no time limit
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 190(5) a public company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names of the members` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 190(5) a public company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names of the members` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 190(5) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the members` AT 1
-- (5), alter the index within 14 days after the alteration of the register (AT 0): 14 is in time, 15 is late
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 190(5) a public company must alter the index within 14 days after an alteration of the register` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 190(5) alter the index to show the alteration made in the register of members` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 190(5) a public company must alter the index within 14 days after an alteration of the register` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 190(5) alter the index to show the alteration made in the register of members` AT 15
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 190(5) a public company must alter the index within 14 days after an alteration of the register` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

§ `s 191: where the register is kept`

-- (a): "if the work of making them up is done at another office of the company in Singapore they may be kept at that other office"
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(a) the register and index may be kept at that other office` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(a) the register and index may be kept at that other office` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): arrangement, the office where the work is done, and in Singapore
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 191(1)(b) the register and index may be kept at the office of that other person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the place as a whole: the registered office, (a) and (b) allow; any other place is a duty not met
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1) the registered office of the public company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1)(a) another office of the company in Singapore at which the work of making them up is done` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1)(a) another office of the company in Singapore at which that work is not done` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1)(b) the office in Singapore of the other person with whom the company has arranged to make them up, at which that work is done` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1)(b) an office in Singapore of that other person at which that work is not done` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1)(b) an office of that other person outside Singapore` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 191(1) the place where the register and index are kept is one the subsection allows` `s 191(1) some other place` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the notice on the first keeping elsewhere, or on a change; 14 days
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the public company must lodge notice with the Registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the public company must lodge notice with the Registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the public company must lodge notice with the Registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the last day for lodging the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the last day for lodging the notice` (Date 25 12 2026) EQUALS Date 8 1 2027
#ASSERT `s 191(2) the notice was lodged within 14 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 191(2) the notice was lodged within 14 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026))
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 191(2) a public company must lodge notice with the Registrar within 14 days` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 191(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register and index are kept, or of the change` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 191(2) a public company must lodge notice with the Registrar within 14 days` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 191(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register and index are kept, or of the change` AT 15
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 191(2) a public company must lodge notice with the Registrar within 14 days` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- (3): the offence, $1,000 and a default penalty
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the public company is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the public company is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the most the public company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the penalty of a fine of $1,000 and a default penalty`
#ASSERT `s 191(3) the most the public company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 192: closing, inspection and copies`

-- (1): "not exceeding 30 days in the aggregate in any calendar year": 30 is allowed, 31 is outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 192(1) the public company may close the register of members or a class of members for the periods` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(1) the public company may close the register of members or a class of members for the periods` 29 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(1) the public company may close the register of members or a class of members for the periods` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(1) the public company may close the register of members or a class of members for the periods` 31 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): a member without charge; any other person on payment of $1 or less
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the register and index must be open to the person's inspection` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the register and index must be open to the person's inspection` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the register and index must be open to the person's inspection` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` FALSE 0.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(2) the charge the company requires for an inspection is one the subsection allows` FALSE 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 192(2) a public company must open the register and index to inspection` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 192(2) a public company must open the register and index to inspection` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 192(2) open the register and index to inspection` AT 2
-- (3): a copy, but "only so far as it relates to names, addresses, number of shares held and amounts paid on shares"
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the person may request a copy of the part of the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the person may request a copy of the part of the register` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the sum required in advance for a page is one the subsection allows` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the sum required in advance for a page is one the subsection allows` 0.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the sum required in advance for a page is one the subsection allows` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 pages at $1 a page is $3; 10 pages at 50 cents a page is $5
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the amount payable in advance for the copy, in dollars` 3 1 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the amount payable in advance for the copy, in dollars` 10 0.5 EQUALS 5
-- request received 1 March 2026: the 21 days begin on 2 March (day 1) and end on 22 March
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the last day for sending the copy` (Date 1 3 2026) 0 EQUALS Date 22 3 2026
-- with a further 10 days the Registrar considers reasonable: 31 days in all, ending 1 April 2026
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the last day for sending the copy` (Date 1 3 2026) 10 EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the copy was sent within the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 22 3 2026) 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 192(3) the copy was sent within the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) 0)
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the copy was sent within the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) 10
#ASSERT NOT (`s 192(3) the copy was sent within the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) 10)
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the company must cause the copy to be sent to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the company must cause the copy to be sent to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 192(3) the company must cause the copy to be sent to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the trace clock counts days after the day of the request (AT 0)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 192(3) a public company must send the requested copy within 21 days` "Acme Holdings Ltd" 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 192(3) send the requested copy of the register to the person` AT 21
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 192(3) a public company must send the requested copy within 21 days` "Acme Holdings Ltd" 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 192(3) send the requested copy of the register to the person` AT 22
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
